{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 756150,
  "courseSlug": "the-complete-guide-to-angular-2",
  "courseTitle": "Angular - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "44116476",
      "title": "Introducing Route Guards",
      "lectureOrder": 296,
      "videoOrder": 282,
      "sourceHash": "5ad3368cebb3169321858f925429077a8b13a0fb0e78cb106420ba72661ac233",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.66,
          "end": 2.91,
          "en": "Now last but not least,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 2.91,
          "end": 4.89,
          "en": "to conclude this section",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 4.89,
          "end": 9.89,
          "en": "where you already learned a lot about Angular's router,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.8,
          "end": 12.93,
          "en": "I wanna conclude this section",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 12.93,
          "end": 16.41,
          "en": "by introducing you to route guards.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 16.41,
          "end": 18.9,
          "en": "The idea behind a route guard is in the end",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 18.9,
          "end": 23.46,
          "en": "that you can define a function in modern Angular",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 23.46,
          "end": 27.6,
          "en": "or in older Angular, a class that has a certain method",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 27.6,
          "end": 31.32,
          "en": "that checks whether a certain navigation action",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 31.32,
          "end": 33.12,
          "en": "should be permitted or not,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 33.12,
          "end": 37.23,
          "en": "so that in the end controls access to a route.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 37.23,
          "end": 40.41,
          "en": "And we could, for example, add such a guard here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 40.41,
          "end": 43.533,
          "en": "to our user tasks component route.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 44.37,
          "end": 46.95,
          "en": "And this guard will then guard this route",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 46.95,
          "end": 49.113,
          "en": "and all its child routes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 50.07,
          "end": 52.86,
          "en": "And you add guards to a route by using",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 52.86,
          "end": 56.844,
          "en": "one of these can properties, canActivate,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 56.844,
          "end": 61.14,
          "en": "canActivateChild, canDeactivate or canMatch.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 61.14,
          "end": 64.2,
          "en": "Now the most versatile guard you can set up",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 64.2,
          "end": 68.55,
          "en": "is the canMatch guard because this guard in the end",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 68.55,
          "end": 72.93,
          "en": "allows you to control whether this entire route",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 72.93,
          "end": 77.1,
          "en": "should be matched by a certain navigation action or not.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 77.1,
          "end": 80.03999999999999,
          "en": "So whether some path that has been entered",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 80.03999999999999,
          "end": 83.493,
          "en": "into the URL should match this route or not.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 84.57,
          "end": 87.39,
          "en": "canActivate is somewhat similar,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 87.39,
          "end": 90.987,
          "en": "but comes one step after canMatch.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 90.987,
          "end": 94.62,
          "en": "The canActivate route will be checked by Angular",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 94.62,
          "end": 97.92,
          "en": "once a route has been identified",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 97.92,
          "end": 101.4,
          "en": "as matching for the currently active path,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 101.4,
          "end": 105.60300000000001,
          "en": "but before the component here has been loaded.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 106.77000000000001,
          "end": 109.5,
          "en": "You'll therefore also often see canActivate",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 109.5,
          "end": 111.75,
          "en": "being used in Angular projects,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 111.75,
          "end": 114.75,
          "en": "but canMatch is a bit more modern.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 114.75,
          "end": 118.11,
          "en": "It has not been part of Angular right from the start",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 118.11,
          "end": 119.91,
          "en": "and is a bit more versatile.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 119.91,
          "end": 123.54,
          "en": "So nowadays if you want to control access to a route",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 123.54,
          "end": 127.47,
          "en": "and its child routes, canMatch is typically the guard",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 127.47,
          "end": 128.883,
          "en": "you might wanna set up.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 129.99,
          "end": 132.27,
          "en": "canActivateChild could be used",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 132.27,
          "end": 136.95,
          "en": "if you wanna activate this route here, this component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 136.95,
          "end": 140.973,
          "en": "but not necessarily the child components of that route.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 141.9,
          "end": 143.74,
          "en": "But here I'll use canMatch",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 144.75,
          "end": 149.75,
          "en": "and all these can properties then take arrays,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 149.82,
          "end": 153.66,
          "en": "arrays of guard functions or classes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 153.66,
          "end": 157.86,
          "en": "though as mentioned, the class approach is a bit older.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 157.86,
          "end": 160.98,
          "en": "And I'll show you how to set up route guards",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 160.98,
          "end": 163.32,
          "en": "as classes in the next lecture.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 163.32,
          "end": 167.7,
          "en": "In this lecture here we'll focus on the more modern function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 167.7,
          "end": 170.493,
          "en": "based approach of defining guards.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 171.75,
          "end": 175.149,
          "en": "And if you wanna add such a canMatch guard to a route",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 175.149,
          "end": 179.88,
          "en": "to control whether it's considered by Angular or not",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 179.88,
          "end": 182.34,
          "en": "for an existing navigation action,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 182.34,
          "end": 185.28,
          "en": "if you want to do that with that function form,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 185.28,
          "end": 188.64,
          "en": "you do that by defining a new function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 188.64,
          "end": 192.12,
          "en": "anywhere in your application, in any file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 192.12,
          "end": 194.433,
          "en": "In this case, I'll name it dummyCanMatch,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 195.81,
          "end": 198.03,
          "en": "though typically you might wanna have",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 198.03,
          "end": 199.44,
          "en": "a more descriptive name,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 199.44,
          "end": 203.97,
          "en": "but here it is really just a dummy demo function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 203.97,
          "end": 207.48,
          "en": "And the type here should be canMatchFn",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 207.48,
          "end": 209.4,
          "en": "and you should then store a function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 209.4,
          "end": 212.49,
          "en": "as a value in that constant.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 212.49,
          "end": 214.28300000000002,
          "en": "So that's a similar approach as I used it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 214.28300000000002,
          "end": 219.09300000000002,
          "en": "for the resolver function to get array TypeScript support.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 220.8,
          "end": 225.78,
          "en": "Now a function qualifies as a canMatch guard function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 225.78,
          "end": 229.14,
          "en": "if it then takes two input parameters",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 229.14,
          "end": 234.14,
          "en": "where the first parameter is information about the route",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 234.21,
          "end": 238.89,
          "en": "that you are trying to match or that you're trying to load.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 238.89,
          "end": 242.1,
          "en": "And the second parameter is a segments parameter,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 242.1,
          "end": 246.963,
          "en": "which is in the end an array of URL path segments.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 248.52,
          "end": 253.26,
          "en": "Now inside of this guard function you can then,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 253.26,
          "end": 257.4,
          "en": "for example, again inject things if you need access",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 257.4,
          "end": 261.06,
          "en": "to some service or anything like that for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 261.06,
          "end": 264.81,
          "en": "And you can then perform any logic of your choice in here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 264.81,
          "end": 267.63,
          "en": "You can for example, all the work with observables",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 267.63,
          "end": 272.1,
          "en": "or anything like that because ultimately you should return",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 272.1,
          "end": 274.05,
          "en": "a boolean in here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 274.05,
          "end": 276.96,
          "en": "True if you want to grant access to a route",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 276.96,
          "end": 279.06,
          "en": "or false if you want to deny it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 279.06,
          "end": 282.54,
          "en": "Alternatively, you could also return an observable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 282.54,
          "end": 286.95,
          "en": "that yields such a boolean, so that would be fine as well,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 286.95,
          "end": 289.68,
          "en": "just as with the resolvers.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 289.68,
          "end": 293.49,
          "en": "There you also could return data or observables",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 293.49,
          "end": 294.78,
          "en": "that yield the data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 294.78,
          "end": 298.5,
          "en": "Here it's the same with booleans.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 298.5,
          "end": 301.29,
          "en": "For example, here we could use Math.random()",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 301.29,
          "end": 304.773,
          "en": "to generate a random value between zero and one.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 305.64,
          "end": 310.64,
          "en": "And I'll store the result in a constant call shouldGetAccess",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 312.42,
          "end": 317.42,
          "en": "and then we could check if should get access is true.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 318.42,
          "end": 321.39,
          "en": "In that case, I want to return true,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 321.39,
          "end": 323.67,
          "en": "else, we might wanna return false.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 323.67,
          "end": 326.07,
          "en": "Or what you typically wanna do,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 326.07,
          "end": 328.32,
          "en": "if you don't want to grant access",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 328.32,
          "end": 331.32,
          "en": "is you might want to redirect the user",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 331.32,
          "end": 334.62,
          "en": "because returning false would indeed deny access,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 334.62,
          "end": 336.75,
          "en": "but it would also kind of break the app",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 336.75,
          "end": 340.95,
          "en": "because no route gets activated then in that case.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 340.95,
          "end": 345.36,
          "en": "So the user would kind of look at some broken page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 345.36,
          "end": 348.12,
          "en": "So what you instead of might wanna do",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 348.12,
          "end": 352.533,
          "en": "is you might wanna return a new RedirectCommand here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 353.4,
          "end": 356.88,
          "en": "And RedirectCommand is something you can import",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 356.88,
          "end": 358.923,
          "en": "from @angular/router.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 360.09,
          "end": 361.68,
          "en": "And it does what the name applies,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 361.68,
          "end": 365.16,
          "en": "you can use it to issue a RedirectCommand,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 365.16,
          "end": 369.54,
          "en": "which will get Angular to navigate to a different page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 369.54,
          "end": 372.3,
          "en": "And that's therefore what you typically might want to do",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 372.3,
          "end": 376.17,
          "en": "instead of returning false because these guard functions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 376.17,
          "end": 379.56,
          "en": "actually do not just allow you to return a boolean,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 379.56,
          "end": 384.06,
          "en": "but also such a RedirectCommand or as mentioned before,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 384.06,
          "end": 389.06,
          "en": "a boolean or this RedirectCommand wrapped in an observable.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 390.42,
          "end": 395.29,
          "en": "Now this RedirectCommand then needs a value of type URL tree",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 396.48,
          "end": 401.48,
          "en": "as an input to describe the destination of the redirect.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 401.61,
          "end": 405.27,
          "en": "And you can easily create such a URL tree",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 405.27,
          "end": 408.993,
          "en": "by injecting Angular Router.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 410.37,
          "end": 414.51,
          "en": "So for that you should inject the router,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 414.51,
          "end": 417.31,
          "en": "which is imported from @angular/router",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 418.47,
          "end": 422.88,
          "en": "because that router then has a parse URL method",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 422.88,
          "end": 426.57,
          "en": "to which you can simply pause a string path",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 426.57,
          "end": 431.57,
          "en": "like /unauthorized or whatever you want here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 432.57,
          "end": 436.59,
          "en": "and that will then be converted to such a URL tree.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 436.59,
          "end": 438.6,
          "en": "And that will ultimately then cause",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 438.6,
          "end": 442.863,
          "en": "a redirect navigation to this path.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 444.75,
          "end": 446.43,
          "en": "Well, and with all that done,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 446.43,
          "end": 451.35,
          "en": "you can use this dummyCanMatch guard function here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 451.35,
          "end": 454.983,
          "en": "and add it as a value to this canMatch array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 456.03,
          "end": 458.22,
          "en": "Just as with the resolvers,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 458.22,
          "end": 460.59000000000003,
          "en": "you shouldn't execute these functions.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 460.59000000000003,
          "end": 463.44,
          "en": "Instead, Angular will do that for you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 463.44,
          "end": 466.40999999999997,
          "en": "and you instead should just point at them.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 466.40999999999997,
          "end": 469.68,
          "en": "And you could also add multiple canMatch guards",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 469.68,
          "end": 472.353,
          "en": "to one at the same route if you needed that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 473.58,
          "end": 477.78,
          "en": "With that, I just want to tweak my code here a little bit",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 477.78,
          "end": 481.14,
          "en": "because at the moment I'll always return true",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
